  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "inputHash": "sha256:0eb62d6f030e2099100de62c1f3ed7cd8ccceb720b55c6edda34ef519767af8b",
    "notes": "The named passenger terminal has its historic western spire, eastern flared roof, arched entrance, turquoise frieze, right turret, attached concourse, boarding canopy and eight whole mapped passenger platforms. The forecourt and track terrace are visual fits to existing map geometry, four standard elevation tiles and ordinary station photos. Rail elevations, dwelling gradients, and entrance dimensions are approximate. The signed model includes the historic headhouse, attached rear concourse, boarding canopy and eight platform islands. The independent Leningradsky and Kazansky terminals and surrounding roads remain separate. Interiors, trains, signs and overhead wiring remain outside the authored scope."
  },
